<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="20987" href="schedule/2020/fall/LA/390/20987.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2020" href="schedule/2020.xml">2020</calendarYear><term id="120208" href="schedule/2020/fall.xml">Fall 2020</term><subject id="LA" href="schedule/2020/fall/LA.xml">Landscape Architecture</subject><course id="390" href="schedule/2020/fall/LA/390.xml">Independent Study</course></parents><sectionNumber>PR </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Health and Urban Landscapes</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This seminar takes a historical perspective on ideas about health, disease, and well-being in urban spaces. Focusing mostly on the United States and Europe from the nineteenth-century we will study the ways that modern ideas about urbanization and landscapes intersected with developments in medicine, public health, thinking about the body, and conceptions of health and quality of life.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2020-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2020-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><instructors><instructor lastName="Rhee" firstName="P">Rhee, P</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>